"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Replacing a sub-adviser without a shareholder vote**\n\nManager-of-managers exemptive relief (Section 15(a), Rule 18f-2, 1940 Act) requires:\n\n- **Board approval:** The board, including a majority of independent directors, approves the new sub-advisory agreement after a 15(c)-style review.\n- **Prior authorization:** Shareholders approved the structure, or the initial prospectus disclosed it before public sale.\n- **Information statement:** Sent to shareholders within about 90 days, often via notice of internet availability.\n- **Limits:** Affiliated sub-advisers usually need specific relief. Any increase in the adviser's fee still requires a shareholder vote.\n\n**What the principal adviser retains**\n\n- Overall management and fiduciary responsibility for the ETF\n- Selecting, monitoring, evaluating and recommending termination of sub-advisers\n- Compliance oversight, including Rule 38a-1 policies\n- Its own advisory agreement, which still requires shareholder approval\n\nConditions vary by order, so check the fund's specific relief.","ttft_ms":5641,"type":"result","duration_ms":7989,"uuid":"9a8a3c61-032c-429f-863d-9ef02a83a326","ttft_stream_ms":484,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":484,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
